            "text": "Outdoor balls usually have around 40 smaller holes, a harder shell and weigh near the top of the legal range, so they fly straight in wind and survive rough courts. Indoor balls usually have around 26 larger holes and a softer feel, which suits smooth gym floors. Using the wrong type changes pace and control noticeably."
